# The CLI's testing workspaces are USER-side too: the tests run `nros sync` /
# `nros deploy` inside them. Several workspaces carry their own `.gitignore`
# with `/build/` and `**/target/`; this covers the kinds none of them named.

# `nros sync` writes a one-line `include = ["…/nros-patch.toml"]` into each
# leaf `.cargo/`, pointing at a gitignored, host-specific central patch file.
**/.cargo/config.toml

# Codegen output — generated from the HOST's message packages, absent from a
# fresh clone. No `Cargo.lock` may be committed beside one either (it would
# name crates nobody has); `check-leaf-lockfiles` enforces that, and this stops
# either from being staged by accident.
**/generated/
